# Copy this file to `gradle.properties` and set the path to your own JDK.
#
# `gradle.properties` is gitignored because this path is machine-specific -- committing it
# would break the build for everyone else.
#
# You need JDK 11 or newer (a JRE will not do). JDK 17 is a good choice: the Gradle wrapper
# here is 7.4, which supports Java up to 17, so 21+ will fail.
# Temurin builds: https://adoptium.net/
#
# Windows example (note forward slashes):
#org.gradle.java.home=C:/Users/you/.jdks/jdk-17.0.20+8
#
# macOS example:
#org.gradle.java.home=/Library/Java/JavaVirtualMachines/temurin-17.jdk/Contents/Home
#
# Linux example:
#org.gradle.java.home=/usr/lib/jvm/temurin-17-jdk
#
# If JAVA_HOME already points at a suitable JDK you can leave this file empty --
# Gradle will use JAVA_HOME instead.
